  "notes": "USAGE:\nCovers both international migration (emigration/immigration) and domestic relocation. In recent years, {移住|いじゅう} has been commonly used in Japan to refer to urban residents moving to rural areas, a trend encouraged by local governments.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {海外|かいがい}{移住|いじゅう}: emigration overseas\n- {地方|ちほう}{移住|いじゅう}: relocation to the countryside\n- {移住|いじゅう}{先|さき}: destination of relocation\n- {移住|いじゅう}{者|しゃ}: immigrant, settler\n- {移住|いじゅう}{支援|しえん}: relocation support",
